139122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1139023-do-garou-mate-in-their-lupus-or-crinos-form?p=1139037#post1139037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> why on earth would they bother?</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps because they would - due to personal reasons, like someone's Glabro, Crinos, and/or Hispo being very attractive and beautiful to their partner - prefer to have sex in forms other than Homid or Lupus? Maybe some would try it out of curiosity and a desire to do something new.<br /> <br /> Also - <i>why</i> wouldn't they bother?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 09-10-2017, 03:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T12:08:01-07:00","id":1139240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicballz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1139023-do-garou-mate-in-their-lupus-or-crinos-form?p=1139103#post1139103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is this seriously why?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Female Garou have their breasts flatten against their chest and largely disappear for the same reason. Ethan Skemp explained this back in the agww newsgroup days, and it may also be mentioned in either the revised Storytellers Handbook or Guide to the Garou IIRC.<br /> <br /> (Fun fact: At least one or more of the ancient Egyptian accounts of Horus, Avenger of His Father, battling Set involve him ripping one of Set's testicles off after Set gouged out Horus's eye.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T12:47:03-07:00","id":1139247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1139023-do-garou-mate-in-their-lupus-or-crinos-form?p=1139066#post1139066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A male garou's <b>gentiles</b> completely retract inside his body while in Crinos, so as there's no risk of them <i>getting torn off</i> during combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>The spelling is genitals and genitalia. The phrase &quot;a male Garou's gentiles&quot; conjures to mind something else entirely, especially if they retract into his body. (^VVVVVV^)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">P<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">erhaps because they would - due to personal reasons, like someone's Glabro, Crinos, and/or Hispo being very attractive and beautiful to their partner - prefer to have sex in forms other than Homid or Lupus? Maybe some would try it out of curiosity and a desire to do something new.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Also - </span></span></span><i>why</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> wouldn't they bother?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Out of the near and combat forms, it's typically only been near-human that can be compatible with humans, as it typically is still in the same size range as most normal humans. Crinos and Hispo, however, are much larger. much more powerful (the unarmed combat maneuver descriptions for W:tA note that a punch or kick from a Crinos werewolf trying not to use claws can still deal lethal damage to a human), and much more inclined to push the Garou in question into frenzy. Having sex in this form is a bad, bad idea, unless, and possibly nonetheless even if, your partner is a receptive variety of spirit or a changeling with a suitably durable kith and you're trysting in some region of the Dreaming that boosts the birthrights that make them durable.<br /> <br /> (4chan likes to talk about using Mage spheres as well. It's almost a regular occurrence on /tg/ WoD general topic threads. I have my doubts that any of these approaches would jive with the ways lots of mages use their Special K...)<br /> <br /> The war form is called that for a reason. It has the capacity to tear enemy and ally alike into bloody gibbets; you probably want to keep it as far away from your allies as possible.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T17:06:01-07:00","id":1139302,"title":"","content":"This is just one big furry-bait threat, right?<br /> Well, I'm bailing!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13654-davesknd","name":"Davesknd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T18:33:43-07:00","id":1139323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray